  "query_preview": "..\nMeteorological Overview:\n\nHigh temperatures in the 80s are possible today, due to weak \nridging aloft with shortwave ridges embedded, coupled with a warm\nfrontal passage this afternoon will cause temperatures to spike \nto potential record breaking values upwards of mid-80s. It will \ndepend on how much diurnal heating can be supplied once cloud \ncoverage scatters out of the region.\n\nAfter a very warm afternoon, a cold front associated with a \ndigging upper trough will bring much cooler air into the CWA this\nweekend. Moisture transport ahead of the upper trough will bring\nin rain beginning Saturday night. \n\nIt is becoming increasingly likely that this incoming weather\nsystem on Sunday will bring at least 0.1 inch of QPF to our CWA,\nwith wetter conditions over the southern zones. Rain is expected \nwith a possible wintry mix. \n\nPrecipitation is expected to move out late Monday.\n\nTuesday and beyond: Drier and somewhat warmer conditions are\nexpected Tuesday. Another system brushes mainly the southeast\nzones Wednesday and Thursday. Temperatures are expected to be near\nseasonable norms. \n\nForecast Confidence & Deviations: \n\nConfidence is low with precipitation type.\n\nConfidence is high with temperatures. \n\nConfidence is low with respect to the track of the low pressure \ncenter Wednesday and Thursday.\n\nFIN",
